// CHECKOUT PROMENADE — AISLE FEVER — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// CHECKOUT PROMENADE as a late-70s disco club mix — a game alternate of shop, selectable
// from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// The fourth shop remix, and the only dance mix of them.
// 
// Peter: "an absolute banger funky disco club mix with funky guitar strumming. Think Good
// Times by Chic." An original groove in that manner, not that record's riff, bass or chords.
// 
// The tune is the shop's, note for note (shop.js lead, bars 7–14), with its harmony line
// and twinkle, on the shop's chords coloured funky, one every half bar:
//   A  | C6/9  Am11 | Dm9  G13 |        (Am11 without the E, under the tune's F)
//   B  | Fmaj9 Em7  | Am7  Dm9 G13 |
// and every phrase's fourth bar anticipating the next chord from its last eighth.
// 120 BPM, swing 52.
// 
// THE GUITARS. One sixteenth-note hand across two FRPP-6 guitars: GUITAR 1 (frppFunkRhythm,
// left) the short accented stabs, GUITAR 2 (frppFunkMuted, right) the muted chucks between
// them; GUITAR 3 (frppFunkBright) high triad chops on the & of 1, a of 2, & of 3, a of 4 in
// the choruses. Each lane strums Alternate (up-strokes 4–5 dB under), which flips on every
// strike of the lane, so each lane's strikes alternate down (an eighth) and up (the
// sixteenth between) from a down — the generator asserts it on every bar. Voicings are
// rootless, one note per string: C6/9 E A D G · Am11 D A C G · Dm9 F A C E · G13 F A B E ·
// Fmaj9 E A C G · Em7 D G B E · Am7 E A C G.
// 
//   1–4    INTRO — guitars 1 and 2 alone; kick and hats at 3; a fill, the bass pickup and
//          a violin swoop at 4
//   5–8    GROOVE — the band: fingered bass jumping octaves, four on the floor, snare on
//          2 and 4, open hats on the off-beats, sixteenth hats, conga; horn answers
//   9–16   VERSE — A then B: the GRAND has the tune an octave up; strings and the vibes on
//          the shop's harmony line for the B; a swoop into
//   17–24  CHORUS — the grand over the VIOLINS an octave under; guitar 3's chops, clap,
//          tambourine, shaker, two congas; horns answering the tune; string stabs
//   25–28  GROOVE 2 — the tune out: guitars, chops, horn riff; a fill and the drums stop
//   29–36  BREAKDOWN — bass and guitars only, on the B changes: stabs every three
//          sixteenths against the chucks, the bass's feature line; at 33 guitar 3 has the
//          B tune at the shop's own pitch
//   37–40  BUILD — the kick back, the violins on the A tune an octave up over the strings,
//          hats opening, a snare roll from eighths to sixteenths, the riser, a swoop
//   41–56  FINAL CHORUS — A B A B, everything; guitar 3 doubles the tune from 49
//   57–64  OUTRO GROOVE — the tune out, the horn riff, the kit thinning, a fill and a swoop
//          back into bar 5
// 
// Pump: the banger styles' rhythmgate (attack 0.16, depth 0.65) on the string pad. The
// loop is bars 5–64. Unrendered and unlevelled: lane gains are set by reasoning, and the
// trailing master gain (-4.4 dB) is an estimate for −21 LUFS.
// 64 bars at 120, 128 s. Written by work/local/_shop-remix-aisle-fever.mjs
// through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
